<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania plans $200 mln eurobond launch mid-March.</title>
<headline>Lithuania plans $200 mln eurobond launch mid-March.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic state of Lithuania said on Friday that it would invite banks to launch a $200 million eurobond.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Rolandas Matiliauskas said in a statement that around 15 international banks had been requested to provide proposals for the bond and a decision on the bank that would arrange the launch would be made in mid-March.</p>
</text>
